"<strong>Planet mass</strong> (Earth masses), from the star’s top speed \\(K\\) (m/s) and the period: change the period to years (days ÷ {#}); take its cube root; separately take the cube root of (star mass)²; then multiply \\(K\\) ÷ {#} by both cube roots. As one formula: mass = (\\(K\\) ÷ {#}) × \\(P^{1/3}\\) × \\(M_s^{2/3}\\), with \\(P\\) in years and \\(M_s\\) in Sun masses.",
